## Convert the cycling time to hours
t &= 1 + \frac{12}{60}
&= 1.2 \text{ hours}
## Find |BA| using distance = speed × time
|BA| &= 25 \times 1.2
&= 30 \text{ km}
## Add the three sections
\text{Total} &= 4 + 30 + 28
&= 62 \text{ km}
ANSWER: 62 \text{ km}

## Use the area with base AB and height d
The shortest distance from $C$ to $AB$ is the perpendicular height $d$ on base $|AB| = 30$.
\frac{1}{2}(30)d &= 50.1
15d &= 50.1
d &= \frac{50.1}{15}
d &= 3.3 \text{ km}
ANSWER: 3.3 \text{ km}

## Use tan in the right-angled triangle TAB
The angle at $B$ is $0.05^\circ$, the side opposite is $|AT| = x$ and the adjacent side is $|AB| = 30$ km.
\tan 0.05^\circ &= \frac{x}{30}
x &= 30 \tan 0.05^\circ
x &= 0.0262 \text{ km}
## Convert to metres
x &= 0.0262 \times 1000
&= 26 \text{ m}
ANSWER: |AT| = 26 \text{ m}

## Use the z-score of a sample mean
$z = \dfrac{\bar{x} - \mu}{s/\sqrt{n}}$ with $\bar{x} = 19.8$, $\mu = 21$, $s = 5.2$, $n = 60$.
z &= \frac{19.8 - 21}{5.2/\sqrt{60}}
&= \frac{-1.2}{0.6713...}
&= -1.787
ANSWER: z = -1.787

## Three non-office keys, then an office key (no replacement)
There are $23 - 5 = 18$ non-office keys. Each key drawn is not put back, so the totals drop by one each time.
P &= \frac{18}{23} \times \frac{17}{22} \times \frac{16}{21} \times \frac{5}{20}
&= \frac{24480}{212520}
&= 0.1152
ANSWER: 0.1152

## Probability of one particular order
P(\text{G, S, O}) &= \frac{12}{23} \times \frac{6}{22} \times \frac{5}{21}
&= \frac{360}{10626}
## Multiply by the number of orders
The three different keys can be drawn in $3! = 6$ orders, each with the same probability.
P &= 6 \times \frac{360}{10626}
&= \frac{360}{1771}
&= 0.2033
ANSWER: 0.2033

## Find the angle at B
The plane turns $20^\circ$ south of east, so the interior angle at $B$ is $180^\circ$ minus $20^\circ$.
|\angle ABC| &= 180 - 20
&= 160^\circ
## Use the sine rule to find |BC|
The side $|BC| = x$ is opposite the angle $8.57^\circ$, and $|AC| = 1450$ is opposite $160^\circ$.
\frac{1450}{\sin 160^\circ} &= \frac{x}{\sin 8.57^\circ}
x &= \frac{1450 \sin 8.57^\circ}{\sin 160^\circ}
x &= 631.7626\ldots \text{ km}
## Convert the distance to a time
Time is distance divided by speed.
\text{Time} &= \frac{631.7626\ldots}{420}
&= 1.504\ldots \text{ hours}
&= 90 \text{ minutes}
ANSWER: 90 \text{ minutes}

## Find the time to fly directly from A to C
\text{Time}_{AC} &= \frac{1450}{420}
&= 3.4523\ldots \text{ hours}
## Find the total flying time in hours
The journey is $A \to B$ (2 hours), $B \to C$ (1.5 hours) and $C \to A$.
\text{Total} &= 2 + 1.5 + 3.4523\ldots
&= 6.9523\ldots \text{ hours}
## Convert the total time to seconds
6.9523\ldots \times 3600 &= 25\,028.57\ldots \text{ seconds}
## Find the fuel needed
\text{Fuel} &= 3.8 \times 25\,028.57\ldots
&= 95\,108.57\ldots \text{ litres}
## Compare with the fuel capacity
$95\,108.57\ldots < 100\,000$, so the plane has enough fuel to complete the journey without refuelling.
ANSWER: 95\,108.57 \text{ litres} < 100\,000 \text{ litres}

## Set the voltage equal to 110
110\sqrt{2}\,\sin(120\pi t) &= 110
\sin(120\pi t) &= \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}
## Solve for the angle
$\sin\theta = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}$ when $\theta = \frac{\pi}{4}$ (one solution).
120\pi t &= \frac{\pi}{4}
## Divide both sides by 120π
t &= \frac{\pi}{4 \times 120\pi}
t &= \frac{1}{480}
ANSWER: t = \frac{1}{480} \text{ seconds}

## Write down the conjugate of $z_1$
Change the sign of the imaginary part.
\bar{z}_1 &= -3 - 4i
## Subtract $z_2$
\bar{z}_1 - z_2 &= (-3 - 4i) - (4 + 3i)
&= -3 - 4i - 4 - 3i
&= -7 - 7i
## Find the modulus using $\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}$
|\bar{z}_1 - z_2| &= \sqrt{(-7)^2 + (-7)^2}
&= \sqrt{49 + 49}
&= \sqrt{98}
&= \sqrt{49 \times 2}
&= 7\sqrt{2}
ANSWER: 7\sqrt{2}

## Identify $a$, $b$ and $c$
Compare with $ax^2 + bx + c = 0$.
a &= 5
b &= -2
c &= -9
## Substitute into the quadratic formula
x &= \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}
&= \frac{-(-2) \pm \sqrt{(-2)^2 - 4(5)(-9)}}{2(5)}
&= \frac{2 \pm \sqrt{4 + 180}}{10}
&= \frac{2 \pm \sqrt{184}}{10}
## Find the first solution
x &= \frac{2 + \sqrt{184}}{10}
&\approx 1.56
## Find the second solution
x &= \frac{2 - \sqrt{184}}{10}
&\approx -1.16
ANSWER: x = 1.56 \quad \text{or} \quad x = -1.16
